<!-- @after 12. Further Reading :: recap -->
### Say these in the interview

- Use one backend intent per order and a stable idempotency key; a timeout never justifies a new charge intent.
- Bind preparation, reconciliation, credentials and poll work to one immutable owner.
- Persist CONFIRMING before presenting PaymentSheet; a callback alone is not payment truth.
- Apply backend revisions atomically and render Room. A stale response or another call’s timeout must not undo a known result.
- After restart, reconcile non-terminal intents; offer continuation for required action and retain pending UX for delayed processing.
